# ⚔️ AETHERIA — PARTY SYSTEM

> **A Party is not simply a group of Heroes.**
>
> **It is a team with a leader, composition, relationships, roles, and combat behavior.**

The **Party System** manages the formation and organization of Heroes before and during missions.

A Party consists of a maximum of:

# **5 Heroes**

The Master controls the overall Party structure, while certain Parties allow a designated Leader to organize their own members.

---

# 1. PARTY SYSTEM OVERVIEW

The Party System manages:

```text
Party Creation
Party Slots
Hero Assignment
Party Leader
Party Composition
Combat Formation
Party Roles
Party Restrictions
Party State
Party Relationships
Party AI
Party Deployment
```

The Party System connects directly to:

```text
Master System
Character / Hero System
AI Character System
Basic Combat System
AI Fairy
Game State System
Database System
ID System
Floor System
Event System
Inventory System
```

---

# 2. PARTY STRUCTURE

Aetheria supports multiple Parties.

Basic structure:

```text
MASTER
  │
  ├── PARTY 1
  │
  ├── PARTY 2
  │
  ├── PARTY 3
  │
  ├── PARTY 4
  │
  └── PARTY ...
```

Each Party has its own:

```text
Party ID
Party Name
Leader
Members
Formation
Party State
Combat State
Mission State
```

---

# 3. PARTY MEMBER LIMIT

Each Party has a maximum of:

```text
5 Heroes
```

Example:

```text
PARTY 1

Slot 1 → Leader
Slot 2 → Hero
Slot 3 → Hero
Slot 4 → Hero
Slot 5 → Hero
```

A Party can contain fewer than 5 Heroes.

Example:

```text
PARTY 2

Slot 1 → Leader
Slot 2 → Hero
Slot 3 → Hero
Slot 4 → Empty
Slot 5 → Empty
```

---

# 4. PARTY SLOT

Each Party contains five possible Hero slots.

```text
┌───────────────────────────────┐
│            PARTY              │
├───────────────────────────────┤
│ SLOT 1 → Leader               │
│ SLOT 2 → Member               │
│ SLOT 3 → Member               │
│ SLOT 4 → Member               │
│ SLOT 5 → Member               │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

Slot position can affect:

```text
Formation
Target Priority
Protection
Combat Position
AI Behavior
Skill Range
```

---

# 5. PARTY 1 & PARTY 2

Party 1 and Party 2 are special Parties.

They have a designated:

# **Party Leader**

The Leader is selected by the Master.

After being appointed, the Leader can manage the composition of their own Party.

```text
MASTER
   │
   ▼
APPOINT LEADER
   │
   ▼
PARTY LEADER
   │
   ▼
SELECT PARTY MEMBERS
   │
   ▼
PARTY COMPOSITION
```

---

# 6. MASTER AUTHORITY

The Master remains the highest authority.

The Master can:

```text
Create Party
Disband Party
Assign Leader
Remove Leader
Change Leader
Move Hero
Remove Hero
Add Hero
Lock Party
Unlock Party
Deploy Party
Recall Party
```

For Party 1 and Party 2, the Master can delegate composition management to the Leader.

---

# 7. PARTY LEADER AUTHORITY

The Leader of Party 1 or Party 2 can manage their own composition.

The Leader can:

```text
Select Members
Remove Members
Change Formation
Set Combat Roles
Recommend Members
Request Hero
Organize Position
```

However:

> **The Party Leader cannot override the Master's authority.**

The Master can always change the Party.

---

# 8. PARTY LEADER SELECTION

The Master selects one Hero as Leader.

Requirements:

```text
Hero must belong to the Master
Hero must be available
Hero must not be locked
Hero must not be assigned to another incompatible Party
```

Example:

```text
MASTER

Assign:

Hero ID:
HERO-000021

Role:
PARTY LEADER

Party:
PARTY-001
```

---

# 9. PARTY LEADER CHARACTERISTICS

The Leader is not necessarily the strongest Hero.

Leadership can depend on:

```text
Personality
Leadership Trait
Experience
Morale
Trust
Relationship
Combat Ability
Strategic Ability
AI Behavior
Master Decision
```

A weak Hero can still become a good Leader.

A powerful Hero may be a poor Leader.

---

# 10. PARTY 1 COMPOSITION

Party 1 allows:

```text
Master
   ↓
Assign Leader
   ↓
Leader manages composition
```

Example:

```text
PARTY 1

Leader:
Leon

Members selected by Leon:

Aria
Mira
Kael
Riven
```

The AI Leader evaluates available Heroes before creating the composition.

---

# 11. PARTY 2 COMPOSITION

Party 2 follows the same special rule.

```text
MASTER
   ↓
ASSIGN PARTY 2 LEADER
   ↓
LEADER
   ↓
SELECT MEMBERS
```

Party 2 can therefore have a different tactical identity from Party 1.

---

# 12. PARTY 3+

Starting from:

# **Party 3**

Party composition is controlled directly by the Master.

```text
PARTY 3+
     │
     ▼
MASTER
     │
     ▼
SELECT HEROES
     │
     ▼
CREATE COMPOSITION
```

The Party Leader delegation system does not automatically apply to Party 3 and above.

